  "assessment": "The change touches four consumers of job status: billing (`charges.py`), retry logic (`retry.py`), SLA duration calculation (`sla.py`), and summary reporting (`summary.py`). It explicitly addresses the ticket by treating cancellation as a terminal event that stops the SLA clock at `ended_at`, prevents retries, waives charges, and tracks the status in summaries. I cannot inspect unmodified files (e.g., queue managers or schedulers) to verify if they also branch on job status, but within the scope of all modified consumers that make decisions based on status, this change is complete.

The SLA fix relies on `st.is_terminal(job.status)` correctly classifying CANCELLED as terminal. The added comments reference `docs/status_lifecycle.md`, confirming that cancellation is a deliberate operator stop and should be treated identically to DONE/FAILED for termination timing.

No defects were found in the provided diff.",
